    "summary": "Water-container (shantali) made of metal, used for ablutions. Stands on hollow conical base with deep flange around the edge, decorated with repoussé work of alternating bands of short strokes and horizontal lines. Body is spherical, upper half of which is stepped. Slender hourglass-shaped neck with wavy spout attached to neck by bar. Single sheet metal side handle runs from mid-body to top of neck where it is hinged to the conical lid. Handle decorated with punched and incised patterns. Domed stopper for spout is attached by chain to joining bar. Container soldered together at mid-body.",
